# Trivy ignore rules
# One ID per line: CVE, secret and misconfiguration check IDs are all accepted.
# Only IDs that are wrong or unfixable for every repository belong here; each one
# suppresses its check repo-wide. Repo-specific exclusions go in that repo's
# trivy.yaml, below the ghb:excluded-dirs block.

# RDS cluster StorageEncrypted is set via Fn::If; Trivy cannot resolve the condition.
AWS-0079
# DocumentDB StorageEncrypted is set via Fn::If; Trivy cannot resolve the condition.
AWS-0021
# Amazon MQ audit logging is ActiveMQ-only; every broker we generate is RABBITMQ.
AWS-0070
# Lambda@Edge does not support X-Ray; every non-edge function has tracing enabled.
AWS-0066
# Unrestricted egress is intentional; workloads need outbound access and ingress is restricted per security group.
AWS-0104
# The API and gRPC load balancers are deliberately internet-facing; they are the public entry point.
AWS-0053
# CloudTrail logs use AWS-managed encryption; a CMK is not required by our baseline.
AWS-0015
# CloudWatch log groups use AWS-managed encryption; a CMK is not required by our baseline.
AWS-0017
# DocumentDB uses the AWS-managed key; a CMK is not required by our baseline.
AWS-0022
# RDS Performance Insights uses the AWS-managed RDS key; a CMK is not required by our baseline.
AWS-0078
# Secrets Manager uses the AWS-managed key; a CMK is not required by our baseline.
AWS-0098
# Buckets use SSE-S3 or the AWS-managed key; ELB access-log delivery constrains the key type.
AWS-0132
# Central log-destination buckets cannot log to themselves; all other buckets have access logging enabled.
AWS-0089
# Multi-Factor authentication is not enforced for group; it is, but Trivy wants an inline policy and we use a customer managed one
AWS-0123
